<title>BAHRAIN: Saudi American Bank H1 net profit up.</title>
<headline>Saudi American Bank H1 net profit up.</headline>
<dateline>MANAMA 1997-07-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30, 1997</p>
<p>			     (million Saudi riyals)</p>
<p> Net profit		505.66   vs     475.05</p>
<p> Operating income    1,544.66   vs   1,580.81</p>
<p> Operating expenses  1,122.29   vs   1,130.37</p>
<p> Other income	     83.28   vs	24.61</p>
<p> Shareholders' funds 4,822.18   vs   4,551.82</p>
<p> Assets		 43,200.79   vs  41,069.65</p>
<p>Full name: Saudi American Bank.</p>
<p>Note - The Riyadh-based bank, the biggest joint venture bank in Saudi Arabia, is 30 percent owned by Citibank unit of U.S. giant Citicorp. The rest is held by Saudi investors.</p>
<p>-- Bahrain newsroom 973-524424.</p>
</text>
